// Tests for stdlib/sha256.caspien: SHA-256 (FIPS 180-4) written in Caspien with the bitwise builtins.
// GENERATED by tests/sha256_gen.py -- every expected digest comes from Python's hashlib (the FIPS vectors "", "abc", the 56-byte
// "abcdbcde...nopq" and one million 'a' are asserted in the generator as well); nothing is typed by hand. Do not edit; edit the generator.
// TABLE-DRIVEN (cases in `let static` arrays, one call site per kind of check, because with function-inlining aggressive each call site
// of `sha256` is a private copy of the hash).
// Covered: the one-shot `sha256` on the standard strings (the 112-byte one, "The quick brown fox...") and one million 'a'; on a patterned
// message of length 0..1000 including every padding boundary (55 56 57 63 64 65 119 120 121 127 128 129 ...); the streaming API
// (`sha256Begin/Update/Finish/Release`) with 7 chunk sizes on 14 lengths, against hashlib AND the one-shot result, plus a million 'a' in
// several splits; the block primitives `sha256Compress` (bytes) and `sha256CompressWords` (16 words) in the exact shapes the Merkle
// benchmark uses (a 16-byte leaf message in one block, a 64-byte node message in two blocks, the second one pure padding) and on padded
// single-block messages; `sha256Init` / `sha256Digest`.
// Prints PASS/FAIL per check and a summary; the output must be identical with every optimisation switch off and on.
import "../stdlib/libc.caspien"
import "../stdlib/sha256.caspien"
import "../stdlib/gt_init.caspien"
import "../stdlib/gt_register.caspien"
import "../stdlib/gt_alive_check.caspien"
import "../stdlib/gt_destruct.caspien"
import "../stdlib/gt_moved.caspien"

